<title>JAPAN: Tokyo Grain Exchange to raise corn futures margins.</title>
<headline>Tokyo Grain Exchange to raise corn futures margins.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-01-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Tokyo Grain Exchange said on Friday it was raising margin requirements for its yen-based corn futures by 20,000 yen, effective from Monday.</p>
<p>The move is aimed at cooling overheated trade, an exchange spokeswoman said.</p>
<p>The margin for the spot March contract will be raised to 260,000 yen, and to 100,000 yen for other contracts. -- Tokyo Commodity Desk +81-3-3432-7391</p>
